From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:09:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: update GE mode atomically

ETHSYS_SYSCFG0 is shared by every MAC.  Updating a single MAC's GE_MODE
field with a whole-register read followed by a write can restore stale
SGMII selection bits changed concurrently by another phylink worker.

Use regmap_update_bits() for the per-MAC GE_MODE field so the regmap lock
serializes it with the existing SGMII path updates.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -786,10 +786,9 @@ static void mtk_mac_config(struct phylin
 		}
 
 		/* put the gmac into the right mode */
-		regmap_read(eth->ethsys, ETHSYS_SYSCFG0, &val);
-		val &= ~SYSCFG0_GE_MODE(SYSCFG0_GE_MASK, mac->id);
-		val |= SYSCFG0_GE_MODE(ge_mode, mac->id);
-		regmap_write(eth->ethsys, ETHSYS_SYSCFG0, val);
+		regmap_update_bits(eth->ethsys, ETHSYS_SYSCFG0,
+				   SYSCFG0_GE_MODE(SYSCFG0_GE_MASK, mac->id),
+				   SYSCFG0_GE_MODE(ge_mode, mac->id));
 	}
 
 	/* SGMII */
